WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.500 --> 00:00:01.920
(Whispers) Don't kill me...please...

00:00:01.920 --> 00:00:02.980
*animatronic scream*

00:00:03.380 --> 00:00:04.260
Fuck-ing...!

00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:06.960
*another animatronic scream, followed by Screamiplier*

00:00:07.440 --> 00:00:09.440
(Nick) It's been years,

00:00:10.620 --> 00:00:11.600
"decades at least,"

00:00:12.040 --> 00:00:13.700
"since I've been inside this house..."

00:00:16.180 --> 00:00:17.860
"I lived here when I was just a kid,"

00:00:17.940 --> 00:00:19.140
"with my family."

00:00:20.260 --> 00:00:20.780
"My mom,"

00:00:21.660 --> 00:00:22.300
"My siblings,"

00:00:22.640 --> 00:00:23.140
"My, uh..."

00:00:23.940 --> 00:00:24.440
"My dad."

00:00:25.860 --> 00:00:30.220
"I received a call from Tobias, telling me that they were finally ready with the repairs this morning..."

00:00:31.400 --> 00:00:32.080
"Took them long enough."

00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:34.860
"Heh."

00:00:35.560 --> 00:00:36.060
"It's funny,"

00:00:36.880 --> 00:00:37.920
"Even after what happened,"

00:00:38.360 --> 00:00:40.080
"in all that time away from home,"

00:00:40.700 --> 00:00:42.660
"it looks just like I remembered it to be."

00:00:43.660 --> 00:00:45.000
"Is my memory that precise?"

00:00:47.640 --> 00:00:48.140
"Ah."

00:00:48.140 --> 00:00:48.680
"Of course,"

00:00:49.180 --> 00:00:50.460
"things like the furniture, and photos,"

00:00:50.780 --> 00:00:51.560
"aren't here anymore,"

00:00:51.980 --> 00:00:52.640
"but hey,"

00:00:53.580 --> 00:00:55.600
"can't blame anybody for that." (Nick chuckles)

00:00:57.060 --> 00:00:57.560
*Nick sighs*

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:00.140
"Right, right..."

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:03.540
"I guess I better use that memory for something useful."

00:01:04.400 --> 00:01:06.480
"I don't have the full story,"

00:01:07.060 --> 00:01:08.260
"nor do I know why it happened..."

00:01:09.200 --> 00:01:09.700
"But,"

00:01:10.240 --> 00:01:11.880
"I can tell you how it started."

00:01:13.700 --> 00:01:16.100
"Everything else is up to you to figure out."

00:01:16.100 --> 00:01:17.600
*Markiplier shrugs and pulls a silly face.*

00:01:17.600 --> 00:01:20.180
"This is the story of the night I lost my home,"

00:01:21.040 --> 00:01:21.860
"my childhood,"

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.080
"and almost my family."

00:01:24.080 --> 00:01:25.280
*Double chin failed attempt*

00:01:25.280 --> 00:01:26.920
"When 'Five Nights at Freddy's'..."

00:01:28.060 --> 00:01:29.460
"...just ended."

00:01:31.180 --> 00:01:31.800
(Mark) Wha-?

00:01:32.960 --> 00:01:33.740
Excuse you?

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:36.120
You gonna get all metaphysical on me?

00:01:36.260 --> 00:01:38.320
Hello everybody! My name is Markiplier, and welcome to

00:01:38.320 --> 00:01:40.140
"The Joy of Creation: Story Mode".

00:01:40.380 --> 00:01:41.760
Now what you saw in the past

00:01:41.900 --> 00:01:45.560
about The Joy of Creation, although it may have been nightmarish,

00:01:45.560 --> 00:01:46.580
was just a taste--

00:01:46.580 --> 00:01:48.720
a demo of what was to come.

00:01:48.720 --> 00:01:51.680
This is the FULL RELEASE of this game,

00:01:51.880 --> 00:01:53.080
and so, going into this,

00:01:53.320 --> 00:01:55.400
I don't even what to expect out of the story.

00:01:55.400 --> 00:01:57.720
Everything that I saw in the earlier opening video

00:01:57.720 --> 00:01:59.320
was just kind of an enigma

00:01:59.320 --> 00:02:01.720
that referred to Five Nights at Freddy's directly;

00:02:01.720 --> 00:02:03.400
I don't know what that means,

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:06.080
so I guess I gotta go into it and find out.

00:02:06.080 --> 00:02:07.880
Le-let's di- *Mark spams LMB*

00:02:07.880 --> 00:02:09.240
Let's dive in.

00:02:09.240 --> 00:02:10.320
I'm trying to--

00:02:10.320 --> 00:02:13.040
*Sudden realization as music plays* Ooooohhhhh...

00:02:13.640 --> 00:02:14.600
Ahhhh.

00:02:14.600 --> 00:02:16.760
"The Bedroom of the Forgotten"? *No, the bedroom's been forgotten, you baka.*

00:02:16.760 --> 00:02:18.480
That sounds morbid. *innit*

00:02:18.480 --> 00:02:19.720
That my bedroom? Oh boy...

00:02:19.720 --> 00:02:21.720
*muffled* Man: Where was he? Where did you see him?

00:02:21.720 --> 00:02:24.520
Mark: Hello...hi... *muffled* Kid: There, there Dad!  Open the door!

00:02:24.520 --> 00:02:26.600
Mark: My name is Markiplier, how are you doing?

00:02:26.600 --> 00:02:27.920
I have hands...

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:31.720
*flashlight clicks on. Clickety click* Man: Uh hello? Um, what are you doing in our house?

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:35.360
Mark: Long story--(muffled voice)--oh.

00:02:35.360 --> 00:02:37.360
*muffled* Kid: Do they look okay?

00:02:37.360 --> 00:02:39.440
Man: Yes, yes he's okay, don't worry

00:02:39.440 --> 00:02:41.520
He just seems, uh, confused?

00:02:41.520 --> 00:02:44.440
Uh ex-excuse me sir, can you tell me your name?

00:02:45.760 --> 00:02:48.400
Look, man, if you won't talk, I'm calling the police.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:50.480
You can't just barge into someone's house like this.

00:02:50.480 --> 00:02:52.640
A-are you hurt? Do you need any help?

00:02:53.240 --> 00:02:54.520
*muffled* Woman: Honey, what's going on?

00:02:54.520 --> 00:02:57.640
*muffled, fading* Man: I don't know, this man 
suddenly appeared in our house

00:02:57.640 --> 00:03:00.760
Nick thought-(indistinct words)-but I don't know... Stay here-

00:03:00.760 --> 00:03:02.260
*growing static sound* Dis guy: MICHAEL!

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:04.260
*muffled* Man: Wh-what?

00:03:04.260 --> 00:03:06.260
Michael:  I, uh, I mean,

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.260
Uh, my name. It's Michael.

00:03:08.260 --> 00:03:10.260
Uh, Michael, I, uh...

00:03:10.540 --> 00:03:12.760
You, you asked me that, before.

00:03:15.020 --> 00:03:18.060
*muffled* Kid: Daddy, Michael kind of sounds like you!

00:03:18.060 --> 00:03:21.220
Woman: Excuse me, but...

00:03:21.220 --> 00:03:22.940
Just what are you doing in our house?

00:03:23.700 --> 00:03:25.380
The sun's about to go down--

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:27.620
I don't think you should be here

00:03:27.620 --> 00:03:29.620
Man: Uh, yeah I was just saying that

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.580
You, uh...you, uh...

00:03:31.580 --> 00:03:34.100
Well, you look a little bit roughed up.

00:03:34.100 --> 00:03:35.020
What happened to you?

00:03:35.620 --> 00:03:37.780
Michael: I, ah, I-I don't know,

00:03:37.780 --> 00:03:40.100
I can't remember.

00:03:40.140 --> 00:03:42.420
I'm sorry, but, but I just...

00:03:42.420 --> 00:03:44.540
I just don't know...

00:03:44.540 --> 00:03:48.140
*muffled* Kid: Michael should get up! The floor is bad.

00:03:48.140 --> 00:03:54.340
Daddy, can we help Michael? Michael can come in, it would be bad if we leave him outside

00:03:54.340 --> 00:03:58.620
Man: Oh, I mean...I...I guess, well can you stand?

00:03:58.620 --> 00:04:03.740
Michael: Uh, uh, I think so...a-a bit, I just feel a bit...

00:04:03.740 --> 00:04:06.300
Uh, dizzy...uh yes, dizzy

00:04:06.300 --> 00:04:08.300
Man: Come on, man, let me help you up.

00:04:09.180 --> 00:04:11.140
Mark: Okay, this seems weird.

00:04:11.420 --> 00:04:14.260
So, a stranger goes into your house, passes out--

00:04:14.260 --> 00:04:16.580
Narrator: After that, Dad carried the stranger to our guest room.

00:04:17.380 --> 00:04:20.740
He thanked me for convincing my parents to let him rest in our house for a night,

00:04:21.460 --> 00:04:23.460
or, at least...while he collected his thoughts.

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:27.500
After that, Mom put me in bed.

00:04:27.500 --> 00:04:29.500
*Mark keeps his finger on his lips, before placing his hands together*

00:04:29.620 --> 00:04:31.540
I can't remember much about Michael,

00:04:31.660 --> 00:04:33.580
But I knew he wasn't a bad person,

00:04:33.580 --> 00:04:36.260
Or...at least he didn't look, you know...

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:37.540
Dangerous.

00:04:37.720 --> 00:04:38.220
Mark: Hmm.

00:04:39.180 --> 00:04:42.100
Narrator: I was young, so I guess I just didn't know any better...

00:04:42.100 --> 00:04:44.060
Certainly didn't know what a burglar was,

00:04:44.300 --> 00:04:45.140
that's for sure.

00:04:45.340 --> 00:04:45.840
Mark: Hmm.

00:04:46.880 --> 00:04:51.840
Narrator: Um...not that I was implying that he was, I never talked to him again after that.

00:04:53.920 --> 00:04:54.520
Well...

00:04:55.320 --> 00:04:57.040
Except for when the storm happened.

00:04:57.920 --> 00:05:01.040
That's when I woke up in my bed, and I saw them...

00:05:01.040 --> 00:05:02.000
*Mark has achieved a new level: Genuinely Interested*

00:05:02.000 --> 00:05:02.680
Mark: "THEM"?

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:04.240
Who's "them"?

00:05:04.240 --> 00:05:06.160
What did Michael bring with him?

00:05:07.040 --> 00:05:09.040
Ff-Straight from "Five Nights at Freddy's"?

00:05:09.040 --> 00:05:11.320
Is that what we're supposed to assume here? Is that what that means?

00:05:11.320 --> 00:05:14.280
Space bar to stand up or sit down, press left click to interact with objects.

00:05:14.280 --> 00:05:16.600
Look up while sitting and hold left click to sleep.

00:05:16.600 --> 00:05:18.600
[X] to continue, [Esc] to not show again.

00:05:18.600 --> 00:05:20.600
I don't know what this is all about, but I'm

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.600
gonnaaa...go for it, I guess?

00:05:23.160 --> 00:05:24.680
Alright, let's do this!

00:05:24.680 --> 00:05:28.200
I guess, harumph, I got it. Oh boy...

00:05:28.200 --> 00:05:30.320
Michael: Uh, hello, hello? Um, Nick?

00:05:30.320 --> 00:05:33.040
Uh, hey, little Nicky! It's me, Michael.

00:05:33.040 --> 00:05:35.360
And hey, you don't say anything back to me, okay?

00:05:35.360 --> 00:05:37.840
There are monsters around that'll hear you if you do.

00:05:37.840 --> 00:05:39.720
Now, don't be scared, Nick, okay?

00:05:39.720 --> 00:05:43.040
Listen to me, and we can defeat those monsters, all right?

00:05:43.040 --> 00:05:48.200
Okay, so these monsters might look, uh, surreal...

00:05:48.200 --> 00:05:52.600
Don't look at them too long, or you'll feel weird and see creepy things.

00:05:52.600 --> 00:05:55.800
When you do, turn on your desk lamp next to your bed-- *click*

00:05:55.800 --> 00:05:57.400
You'll feel safe there.

00:05:57.400 --> 00:06:01.160
But the more you stare at the scary monsters, the worse you'll feel, alright?

00:06:01.160 --> 00:06:03.520
Uh, um *thunder*

00:06:03.520 --> 00:06:05.720
Okay, first things first, uh...FREDDY,

00:06:05.720 --> 00:06:07.720
the fuzzy brown bear.

00:06:08.240 --> 00:06:11.360
Uh, he's at the window, and, uh, he'll peek inside...

00:06:11.360 --> 00:06:15.000
Close your curtains, and KEEP them closed until you hear him leave,

00:06:15.000 --> 00:06:17.000
Or else, he'll get inside.

00:06:17.720 --> 00:06:21.000
Uh, then, there's BONNIE, the ill-tempered big purple bunny.

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:23.680
Uh, keep an eye on your door, he'll be there.

00:06:23.680 --> 00:06:25.760
Uh, he's not shy at all.

00:06:25.760 --> 00:06:28.600
He will knock on the door to let you know he's there.

00:06:29.160 --> 00:06:32.560
Once he opens the door, shut off the lights as fast as you can, Nicky;

00:06:32.560 --> 00:06:35.280
he can't see you well in the dark and he'll leave.

00:06:35.280 --> 00:06:38.000
Oh, but make sure you're sitting down when you do that, alright?

00:06:38.000 --> 00:06:39.940
Okay, uhh, then, there's the chicken...

00:06:39.940 --> 00:06:42.500
Um, that one's a little bit weird...

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:44.500
Um, ah, check the closets often.

00:06:44.500 --> 00:06:47.540
Uh, if she's peeking through, make sure to disable the lights.

00:06:47.540 --> 00:06:50.500
Uh, she doesn't want to be seen, but ignoring her doesn't help either

00:06:51.000 --> 00:06:55.660
If she does catch you with the lights on, she'll scare you and stun you.

00:06:55.660 --> 00:06:59.040
*sigh* I know this is a lot to take in little Nicky okay?

00:06:59.040 --> 00:07:02.800
J-ju-just listen carefully and try to remember everything please.

00:07:02.800 --> 00:07:04.400
Mark: OKAY!

00:07:04.400 --> 00:07:06.900
Michael: *sigh* All right, last is FOXY.

00:07:06.900 --> 00:07:07.400
Mark: UEH!

00:07:07.400 --> 00:07:08.780
Michael: He'll be right be right beneath your bed.

00:07:08.780 --> 00:07:09.280
Mark: UGH!!

00:07:09.280 --> 00:07:11.400
Michael: You'll hear scraping from the bottom of the crib when he's there.

00:07:11.400 --> 00:07:11.900
Mark: Uh...

00:07:11.900 --> 00:07:14.900
Michael: Uh, be watchful if you see his hook on the back of your bed,

00:07:14.900 --> 00:07:17.740
'Cause soon enough, he'll be right there next to the bed.

00:07:17.740 --> 00:07:19.740
Don't look directly at him, Nick--

00:07:19.740 --> 00:07:21.740
Instead, pretend to sleep,

00:07:21.740 --> 00:07:25.380
all right? Just pretend to sleep, yeah, just lie down without moving too much.

00:07:25.380 --> 00:07:27.860
Look up and close your eyes.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:31.820
Uh, Foxy sees eyes as if they're *click* big, bright *thunder* spotlights,

00:07:31.820 --> 00:07:35.420
okay? So if you pretend to sleep, he won't know that you're there anymore.

00:07:35.420 --> 00:07:38.820
But don't open them until you know that he's gone, okay?

00:07:39.580 --> 00:07:42.100
Okay, uh, so, to recap, um...

00:07:42.100 --> 00:07:46.460
Freddy is at the window, so if you see him peeking, close the curtains until he's gone.

00:07:46.460 --> 00:07:49.820
Uh, Bonnie will knock at the door and open it afterwards;

00:07:49.820 --> 00:07:52.500
uh, disable the lights and sit down until he leaves.

00:07:52.500 --> 00:07:57.100
Chica will try to stun you by scaring you, so if you see her peeking through the closet,

00:07:57.100 --> 00:08:00.060
shut off your lights and don't pretend to sleep--

00:08:00.060 --> 00:08:01.660
she'll think you're gone.

00:08:01.660 --> 00:08:05.340
And Foxy will appear under your crib and move upwards,

00:08:05.340 --> 00:08:09.620
so when he's next to your bed, pretend to sleep until you hear him leave.

00:08:09.620 --> 00:08:10.120
Mark: Huh?

00:08:10.120 --> 00:08:11.280
Michael: Alright, you got all that?

00:08:11.280 --> 00:08:11.780
Mark: No!

00:08:11.780 --> 00:08:15.280
Michael: Alright, good, uh, listen I have to go little buddy, okay?

00:08:15.280 --> 00:08:17.660
Just hang in there, they'll leave at 6:00 AM, I'm sure of it.

00:08:17.660 --> 00:08:19.180
You can do this-- *Gets cut off.*

00:08:21.260 --> 00:08:23.980
Mark: Uh-uhh you're just going to be cut off right then and there?

00:08:23.980 --> 00:08:26.740
And I'm going to be left alone with THAT information?!

00:08:27.260 --> 00:08:29.500
*click* I've got to deal with all of them right a-waaay *sees something*

00:08:30.380 --> 00:08:30.880
Hello?

00:08:31.600 --> 00:08:32.100
*click*

00:08:32.180 --> 00:08:33.020
I have no idea...

00:08:33.300 --> 00:08:34.700
I can't remember which is which.

00:08:34.700 --> 00:08:36.620
Swing-swong the swing swong for Freddy

00:08:36.620 --> 00:08:38.100
Uhh, lights off for Bonnie and Chica,

00:08:38.100 --> 00:08:39.540
but I don't--wait--I--no!

00:08:39.540 --> 00:08:41.580
Nah, ah, lights ON for Chica.

00:08:41.580 --> 00:08:42.080
Uh...

00:08:42.880 --> 00:08:45.880
I have no idea what any of this is about or what I'm suppose to be doing here.

00:08:46.440 --> 00:08:48.520
UhhhHHHHAAAAHHHHhh-kay

00:08:48.880 --> 00:08:49.380
*click*

00:08:51.740 --> 00:08:54.260
I don't remember, am I suppose to keep that light on for ANY

00:08:54.260 --> 00:08:56.780
Par *thunder* ticular reason? *Yes, it keeps you sane, Mark*

00:08:57.420 --> 00:08:58.380
Any at all?

00:08:59.180 --> 00:08:59.680
Nope?

00:08:59.680 --> 00:09:00.960
Okay. *click* All right.

00:09:01.800 --> 00:09:05.200
We're just going to pretend like everything's okay, and I'm not about to DIE!

00:09:06.000 --> 00:09:06.800
Uhhh.

00:09:07.280 --> 00:09:09.600
What is that? I see something over--oh, *click* that's a branch?

00:09:09.880 --> 00:09:10.720
Is that a branch?

00:09:10.720 --> 00:09:11.220
*boom*

00:09:11.220 --> 00:09:11.720
Ah!

00:09:12.440 --> 00:09:14.160
THAT'S A BRAN-NOT A BRANCH! *click*

00:09:14.160 --> 00:09:15.160
WHAT ARE YOU?!

00:09:15.160 --> 00:09:17.400
Euh, I don't *thump* knoOAAYYYYY! *thump*

00:09:18.440 --> 00:09:21.160
I, uh, okay! I guess I gotta *click* turn that off and SIT DOWN!

00:09:23.460 --> 00:09:25.460
*Window opens.*

00:09:26.000 --> 00:09:27.440
Oh, that's not good...

00:09:27.440 --> 00:09:28.500
*Jumpscare in 3...*

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.400
*Jumpscare in 2...*

00:09:29.400 --> 00:09:30.140
*Jumpscare in 1...*

00:09:30.140 --> 00:09:31.060
EuuaAHH

00:09:31.060 --> 00:09:32.580
*Mechanical scream* AHHH!

00:09:42.980 --> 00:09:43.480
*sigh*

00:09:43.480 --> 00:09:45.480
Let's try that again, shall we?

00:09:46.480 --> 00:09:48.240
I don't know what I needed to do...

00:09:48.240 --> 00:09:51.080
Just gonna do this trial by error, because I don't think...

00:09:51.520 --> 00:09:53.160
I don't think it's gonna MATTER what I do

00:09:53.160 --> 00:09:55.200
because I think I'm going to die no matter what,

00:09:55.200 --> 00:09:56.720
so, let's just do this.

00:09:56.720 --> 00:09:58.640
I think I remember it, if I don't,

00:09:58.640 --> 00:10:01.340
ha, I'll just die, I'll keel over and die.

00:10:01.340 --> 00:10:01.940
*nervous laugh*

00:10:01.940 --> 00:10:03.940
That'll be great. Actually, I won't keel over and die

00:10:03.940 --> 00:10:07.420
I'll have my soul ripped outta my body by animatronics.

00:10:07.420 --> 00:10:11.140
Alright, it's for Freddy, only when you see him, do you turn... *click*

00:10:11.700 --> 00:10:13.700
Turn, da, the curtains close.

00:10:13.700 --> 00:10:16.300
Turn off the curtains. You gotta turn off the curtains for Freddy.

00:10:16.620 --> 00:10:18.620
That's how that works and that's how logic is.

00:10:18.620 --> 00:10:20.620
And then for Bing-bong on the door-door,

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:22.620
You gotta turn out the lights and make Bonnie go bye-bye.

00:10:23.140 --> 00:10:24.060
Ohhh-hi.

00:10:24.060 --> 00:10:24.860
'Scuse you,

00:10:24.860 --> 00:10:25.780
what is that?

00:10:26.180 --> 00:10:27.420
I don't know what that is.

00:10:30.900 --> 00:10:32.820
I don't know what you are!

00:10:33.460 --> 00:10:33.960
Is he there?

00:10:33.960 --> 00:10:34.460
AH!

00:10:34.460 --> 00:10:35.540
Ohhhhhh

00:10:36.340 --> 00:10:37.820
Don't play peek-a-boo with me.

00:10:38.180 --> 00:10:38.980
Okay, alright.

00:10:39.300 --> 00:10:40.740
Well? That's one, for ME

00:10:40.740 --> 00:10:42.540
in the win column!

00:10:42.540 --> 00:10:44.300
A lot of losses but still, you know?

00:10:44.300 --> 00:10:45.700
At least I'm in the game.

00:10:46.060 --> 00:10:46.560
Uh.

